# STAGING build (npm run build:staging → ag-warriors-hero-staging)
#
# Deliberately EMPTY: with no Supabase credentials the app falls back to its
# built-in mock mode (see src/lib/supabase.ts → supabaseReady). That makes
# staging a zero-risk UI playground — it CANNOT touch live warrior data.
#
# These blank values also override .env.local, which holds the production
# credentials and is otherwise loaded in every mode.
#
# To make staging a full environment later: create a SECOND Supabase project,
# run supabase/migrations/BOOTSTRAP.md against it, and paste its URL + anon key
# below. Never point staging at the production project.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
